      "message": "Hello Patryk,\nJust confirming that I understand your comment:\n\u003e\u003e No. Somebody could rely on that behavior. \n[FS] Do you mean someone can reply on this bahavior in the upstream?\n\n\u003e\u003e You can create exit.c file and implement _exit that does what you want.\n[FS] Exactly, I tried to place that function in a source file that compiles with the exit test. Specifically, I added it as an experiment in `platform/ec/common/panic_output.c` and it does override the weak function\n\nNow my question, is where in our zephyr implementation can we override the exit function? Is there a specific location that you recommend? My understanding, this is going to be contained in out implementation and is not part of the zephyr upstream",
